 **//*
	 * These IRQ flags must be cleared when we start as stop_traffic()
	 * relys on them to indicate when activity has stopped.
	 *//* Start receive *//* Start transmit *//* Start rxp + txp *//* Clear out EMAC interrupts *//* Stop rxp + rxp *//* Stop receive *//* Stop transmit *//* Lookup priority order: DPI -> VLAN -> IP proto -> FWT *//* multicast redirect target node *//* 0 = multicast judgement based on emac core status, not DA *//*
	 * EMAC RXP has 8 registers for DSCP -> TID mappings. Each register has 8 nibbles;
	 * a single nibble corresponds to a particular DSCP that could be seen in a packet.
	 * There are 64 different possible DSCP values (6 DSCP bits).
	 * For example, register 0's nibbles correspond to:
	 * Reg mask 0x0000000f -> DSCP 0x0. Mask is ANDed with the desired TID for DSCP 0x0.
	 * Reg mask 0x000000f0 -> DSCP 0x1
	 * ...
	 * Reg mask 0xf0000000 -> DSCP 0x7
	 * Next register is used for DSCP 0x8 - 0xf.
	 *//* Clear any pending interrupts *//* In order to drop a packet, the following conditions has to be met:
		 * emac_xflow_disable == 1
		 * skb->skb_iif has to be none zero
		 * skb->skb_iif the interface is Rx from emac0 or emac1
		 *//*
	 * restore VLAN tag to packet if needed
	 *//* drop any WBSP control packet towards emac1 (Ethernet type 88b7)
	Quantenna OUI (00 26 86) is located at data[14-16] followed by 1-byte type field [17] *//*
		 * For each transmitted buffer, TQE will update:
		 * - tdes1 (control) according to TOPAZ_TQE_EMAC_TDES_1_CNTL & payload size
		 * - tdes2 (bufaddr1) with payload dma address
		 * So initializing these fields here is meaningless
		 *//* discard WBSP control packet coming from emac1 (Ethernet type 88b7)
	Note that in this receive routine, header has been removed from data buffer, so
	Quantenna OUI (00 26 86) is now located at data[0-2] followed by 1-byte type field [3] *//* Stop the emac, try to take the null buffer off and refill with new buffer *//* Stop rxp + emac rx *//* Stop the emac, try to take the null buffer off and refill with new buffer *//* Start rxp + emac rx *//* ARP *//* ethhdr->h_proto: ETH_ALEN*2/sizeof(dword)*//* 8021Q && ARP *//* IPv4 && UDP && srcport == 67 && dstport == 68 *//* src_port/dst_port *//* IPv6 && UDP && srcport == 547 && dstport == 546 *//* IPv6 && ICMPv6 *//* CONFIG_IPV6 *//* Allocate device structure *//* Initialize device structure fields *//* Initialize private data *//* Map the TQE port to the device port *//* Initialize MII *//* Allocate descs & buffers *//* Register device *//* Send EMAC through soft reset *//* The HGW-500BNA RAM handoff is explicitly non-bonded.  Compiling the
	 * dormant bonding path would create an unusable dependency from this GPL
	 * netdev module onto the OEM proprietary fwt_ctrl module. *//* Don't multicast to both ports if they are bonded *//* Create sysfs for dscp misc operations *//* We only use rtl switch as PHY, do not do reset which will restore
	 * to switch mode again. Only do so when using rtl ethernet tranceiver.
	 *//* Reset ext PHY. This is for bug#11906 *//**
