 **//* Default irq handler for unclaimed interrupts *//* Copy the handler structure *//* Copy the handler structure *//* Install an empty handler so we can avoid checking         *//* if a handler is installed every time we take an interrupt *//* Called by the high priority input to kill off the host and
 * prevent it locking up.
 *//* high IPC*//* MuC ask to restart system.
		 *//* touch uc print buffer work queue to flush shared message buf *//* low IPC*//* Call the handlers *//* We are done - See you next time *//* Call the handlers *///			printk("Interrupt for irq %d dev %p\n", i, dev_id);/* We are done - See you next time *//* Reset the MAC data structure *//* Initialize *//* Clear all the interrupt handlers *//* Set interrupts to low (IRQ) priority *//* Set up pointer to int status register for generic int handler *//* Set up pointers for LHost to DSP communication *//* Register handler with linux for MuC interrupt line. *//* Enable the high priority interrupts *//**
