	 * Min. quality is noise + 1 *//* XXX query driver to find out supported key sizes *//* 40-bit *//* 104-bit *//* 128-bit *//* Skip legacy rates *//* estimated maximum TCP throughput values (bps) *//* Event capability (kernel) *//* Event capability (driver) *//* for now, only ibss, ahdemo, sta has this cap *//* for sta only *//* this is used for reporting replay failure, which is used by the different encoding schemes *//* report supported WPA/WPA2 capabilities to userspace *//* save the list of node addresses *//* get the addresses into the driver *//* copy the MAC addresses into a list *//* extract the MAC addresses *//* init rssi timestamps *//*
	 * locate nodes by mac (ieee80211_find_node()),
	 * copy out rssi, set updated flag appropriately
	 *//* locate a node, read its rssi, check if updated, convert to dBm *//* check we are associated w/ this vap *//* copy results to userspace *//* Enhanced iwspy support *//* get the threshold values into the driver *//* disable threshold *//* We are passed a signal level/strength - calculate
		 * corresponding RSSI values *//* XXX: We should use current noise value. *//* set threshold values *//* copy results to userspace *//* XXX: These values, flags, and caps do not seem to be used elsewhere
	 * at all? *//* XXX *//* XXX *//*
