		 *        would mark the channel as unusable is the radar indication
		 *//* Mark the channel as not_available and ready for cac *//* Remove the CSA IE from beacons and cause other field in beacon updated *//* record channel change event *//*
 * Start a CSA process: CSA beacon/action will be sent to STA to notify the CS.
 * @finish_csa: At the CS time, finish_csa() will be called to do the actual CS. If not provided,
 * ieee80211_finish_csa() will be called as default action.
 * @flag: specify whether to use CSA beacon or CSA action or both.
 *//* now flag the beacon update to include the channel switch IE *//* send broadcast csa action *//* Update beacon to include CSA IE *//*
	 * Store original attenuation to handle the following case:
	 * We switched to low power channel when attenuation is small. But then in low
	 * power channel attenuation increases but interference is low. We need to detect
	 * such rate ratio drop to trigger channel ranking.
	 *//* for dfs reentry demon *//*
 * Generate an interference mitigation event
 *//* Choose the channel with maximal power setting *//* All powers are same, run random selection per request *//* There is a potential race condition here, but the timer will kick in and recover it.
	 * Currently we don't plan to protect against it *//*
 * Interference mitigation sampling task
 * Periodically go off-channel to sample the quality of another channel.
 *///FIXME check threshold/* Only sample if at least one VAP is in run state and none are scanning *//* Currently we don't apply the thresholds of FAT and preamble error to QHop case *//* For STA mode, always send cca report to AP *//* Don't switch channel under basic WDS mode *//* But channel switch is now possible on the WDS link if it is an MBS *//* set to -1 helps to discard first report after assoc or channel switch *//*
 * Clean SCS state with different clean levels.
 * Valid levels are IEEE80211_SCS_STATE_XXXX.
 * @clear_dfs_reentry: only effective at level IEEE80211_SCS_STATE_PERIOD_CLEAN.
 *//*
	 * No need to do clean node in level IEEE80211_SCS_STATE_PERIOD_CLEAN
	 * because it is associated with jiffies. So that we don't need to iterate
	 * all node every scs interval.
	 *//* Currently we don't support BRCM 11AC STA's CC request*//* reset entry *//* always scale cca_intf so that it is adaptive to cca duration change and off-chan sample *//* current channel's cca_intf use maximum of AP and STAs *//* update off-channel sampling stats with exponential smoothing *//* only have AP side off-channel sampling now *//* only have AP side off-channel sampling now *//* let sta side pmbl smoothing out *//* mark channel entry updated so it won't be aged out *//*
 * This function should NOT be called right after the txpower change because the rssi may come
 * from the original txpower. Make sure txpower and rssi is match.
 *//* get recent and smooth *//* exponential smooth *//* report smoothed one to ranking database *//* clear the attenuation summary stats before collecting from nodes *//* let all node update their own information into the ranking stats database *//* ms *//* ms *//* ms *//* ms *//* ms *//* ms *//* Add some compensation because (tx_time+rx_time) always is less than the caused cca interference *//* if only downstream traffic or no traffic, don't add compensation *//*  calculate compensation *//* get other nodes' tx/rx time and smooth them *//* old smooth value *//* smooth cca interference *//*
		 * Add some compansation since training packets could
		 * cause high interference in bad environment
		 *//*
		 * We must confirm all of CCA actions are received and all of CCA info are correct,
		 * or we will get wrong total TDLS link time and calculate wrong CCA interference
		 *//* Add some compensation *//* Smooth rising up; but sharp drop *//*
	 * Currently only reset current channel's cca_intf, because other channel's cca_intf
	 * are updated more slowly.
	 *//* collect interference info from all stas *//* traffic condition *//* new smooth value *//* This is used to compensate for RBS *//* inteference condition *//* vendor specific handle *//* PMP case *//* stats is unstable, ignore it *//* remove the interference that come from other associated station *//* Is this node a non-WDS node ? *//* don't record it *//* Handle loaded and idle cases *//* Adjust self intf on mbs-wds *//* update self's *//* Recheck the interference detected by AP self *//*
 * Calculate the rate ratio based on attenuation
 * return unit: percent
 * If no attenuation available, return 100
 * For domains other than us, return 100
 * Otherwise, calculate rate ratio according to attenuation.
 */// percent/* qtn *//* non-qtn, based on test of brcm sta *//* currently only use worst case *//* Correct channel metric to account for different channel switch margins *//* metric preference: power.random *//* Add a little noise to equally choose best ones *//*
 * Channel ranking and selection of SCS
 * Called when SCS decided that channel change is required.
 * Return the selected channel number. 0 means no valid better channel.
 *//* Prepare the information we need to do the channel ranking *//* ranking *//*
		 * (i) When scs_pick_channel is being called from scs comparison task, scs manual,
		 * we should choose from channels which are available
		 * (ii) When scs_pick_channel is being called from OCAC task
		 * we should choose from DFS channels which are not available, cac not done, and radar not detected.
		 *//* This is called only from SCS Manual and SCS comparison task context *//* OCAC needs a DFS channel for which CAC is not already done *//* only calculate channel pair when low number 20M channel is already calculated *//* select worse channel as primary channel within the chan pair *//* only calculate channel set when all 20M channels are already calculated *//* select worst channel as primary channel within the best chan set *//* Need to calculate DFS channel metric in case current channel is DFS channel *//* All the sub-channel can't be primary channel *//* radar detected on this channel, secondary channel or secondary 40MHz channels*//* Weather channel has low priority since it need too long CAC time *//* Select best channel *//* Update best alternate channel information for fast switch *//* If the IEEE80211_CHAN_HT40D channel in 40MHz or IEEE80211_CHAN_VHT80_UU
				 * channel in 80MHz is disabled, curr_metric may be SCS_MAX_RAW_CHAN_METRIC
				 * per above metric calculation, so need to read it from as_chanmetric table.
