				 * don't add preamble failure counts to compound_cca_intf because
				 * the preamble failure counts got by scanning are not reliable
				 *//*
				compound_cca_intf = ieee80211_scs_fix_cca_intf(ic, NULL, scan_info.cca_intf,
						scan_info.spre_err, scan_info.lpre_err);
				*//* clear initial channel ranking table *//* When request is because of interference *//* don't clear dfs reentry and wait for next interval result *//* Copy scs info into a local structure so MuC can continue fill it *//* make sure cross channel switching stats are cleared *//* Read and process off channel stats *//* Scale co-channel data *//* update smoothed free airtime *//* clear current cca intf at first *//* update cca intf stats *//* update tx/rx time stats *//*
			 * Pick a channel from DFS and Non-DFS set of channels;
			 * Consider channel margins as well while we pick the channel
			 *//* In RBS mode - inform the MBS AP to change the channel *//* WDS Link to MBS? *//* here replace the old csa mgmt packet sending*//* In STA mode - inform AP to change the channel *//* STA should be associated *//* here replace the old csa mgmt packet sending*//*
		 * Pick a channel from DFS and Non-DFS sets;
		 * If the picked channel is non-DFS, OCAC performs off-channel CAC for DFS channel;
		 * If the picked channel is DFS, OCAC will not kickin
		 *//* CCA information cannot match a certain channel under scan state *//* Copy scs info into a local structure so MuC can continue to fill it in *//* SCS off channel sampling follows SCS *//* CCA information cannot match a certain channel under scan state *//* Copy scs info into a local structure so MuC can continue to fill it in *//* the ranking table *//* For the scoring, the algorithm as below:
	 *   1. For the channel which has the minimum valid metric, the score is 100
	 *   2. For the channel which has the maximum valid metric, the score is 0
	 *   3. For other channels that have valid metrics, the score is
	 *         100 * (max_valid_metric - metric) / (max_valid_metric - min_valid_metric)
	 *   4. For invalid metric, if it is larger than maximum valid metric, the score is 0;
	 *      and if it is less than minimum valid metric - it may result from too large
	 *      power difference from the current channel, the score is 100.
	 *//* when in auto channel scanning *//* the ranking table *//* WAR for bug16636, supposed to be removed after cca threshold re-tuned *//* QSCS_ENABLED *//* QTN_BG_SCAN *//* QTN_BG_SCAN *//* 80+80 or 160 Mhz *//* Copy HT rates *//* check length, set macaddr, ssid, channel, rssi, flags,htcap*//* ap mac addr *//* ssid *//* channel ieee *//* max bandwidth *//* rssi *//* flags:privacy *//* htcap available *//* vhtcap available *//* check length, copy wpa_ie, wsc_ie and rsn_ie to buffer if exist *//* keep address 4-byte aligned*//* get bit rates from ic->ic_sup_rates[ic->ic_des_mode] *//* Skip legacy rates *//* initialize ap_scan_iter *//*
