 * This function will be called when processes write following command:
 *  get <unit> assoc_info.
 * into file in sysfs.
 *
 * This function is to report all nodes in the table. User can do further filtering.
 * E.g. user only need MAC address on designated WiFi interface.
 *
 * This function works for both AP and STA.
 *//* Unit: in Kbps *//* Unit: second, 32bits should be up to 136 years *//* correct pseudo RSSIs that apparently still get into the node table *//* NOTE: if this output format changes, there are flow-on effects to qcsapi. *//* Unit: second, 32bits should be up to 136 years *//* correct pseudo RSSIs that apparently still get into the node table *//* Kbps *//* Kbps */// Apply WAR for single STA only// check for brcm node with RSSI > rssi_threshold/*
	 * Apply contraint WAR for higher channels only.
	 * The backoff dB value comparing with max reg tx power is a safety check
	 * to make sure the STAs local_tx_power won't be less than 0dBm
	 *//* Back down the STA power using Power constraint *//* Back down the STA power using Secondary Power constraint *//*
 * Implementation of ioctl command: IEEE80211_IOCTL_GET_ASSOC_TBL
 * This command is to report all nodes in the table. User can do further filtering nodes.
 * E.g. user only need MAC address on designated WiFi interface.
 *
 * This function works for both AP and STA.
 *//* Unit: Kbps *//* Unit: second, 32bits should be up to 136 years *//* Correct pseudo RSSIs that apparently still get into the node table *//* The node iterator may hold scan/node locks. Keep all user access outside. *//* Never dereference the userspace ioctl pointer directly. *//*
	 * qcsapi's association-count query requests the complete legacy station
	 * table through SIOCDEVPRIVATE+0xb. Linux holds RTNL around that ioctl and
	 * the legacy implementation then acquires the scan and node-table locks.
	 * On the HGW recovery path the common zero-client poll needs none of that
	 * work. Return the already-maintained count without entering the nested
	 * iterator. Nonzero tables retain the OEM implementation unchanged.
	 *//* All scan/node locks have been released before this single user copy. *//*
		 * Just remove the fdb entry form bridge module,
		 * delay the node free in later node_expire timer callback.
