 *//*
 * Header file which describes Ruby platform.
 * Has to be used by runtime firmware.
 *//* FIXME: Move CPU related macros to a separate header file. *//* NEVTBD - put in real XYMEM values *//* SRAM layout *//* dedicated SRAM space for HBM pointer pools *//* sizeof(void *), 32 bit arch *//* MU TxBF qmatrix is stored at the last bank of SRAM, DSP writes to it, has to use SRAM BUS addr *//* TODO FIXME - MuC crashed when copying data between SRAM and DDR *//* DDR layout  *//* keep it 2^n *//* one for all FF addresses *//* sizeof(struct topaz_fwt_sw_ipmap) *//* sizeof(struct topaz_fwt_sw_mcast_entry) *//* Tables are cache-line aligned to ensure proper memory flushing. *//* Offset from DDR beginning, from which memory start to belong to Linux *//* Linux kernel u-boot image start address, for uncompressed images *//* Linux kernel image start *//* AuC tightly coupled memory specification *//* BBIC4 RevB AuC DMEM bottom 4KB: 0xE510_0000 to 0xE510_0FFF is aliased with Wmac1 TCM 0xE514_0000
 * exclude the bottom 4K from DMEM, and reduce the size from 16KB to 12KB
 *//***************//* Utility functions *//*GCC*//* Kernel is compiled with -mlong-calls option, so we can make calls between code fragments placed in different memories */// #ifndef MUC_BUILD// #ifndef MUC_BUILD// #if RUBY_MUC_TLB_ENABLE/*MCC*/// #ifndef __ASSEMBLY__/*
 * "Write memory barrier" instruction emulation.
 * Ruby platform has complex net of connected buses.
 * Write transactions are buffered.
 * qtn_wmb() guarantees that all issued earlier and pending writes
 * to system controller, to SRAM and to DDR are completed
 * before qtn_wmb() is finished.
 * For complete safety Linux's wmb() should be defined
 * through qtn_wmb(), but I afraid it would kill performance.
 *//*GCC*//*MCC*//*ARC7*//*r12 is temporary register, so we can use it inside this function freely*//*
 * Problem - writing to first half of cache way trash second half.
 * Idea is to lock second half.
 * Need make sure that invalidation does not unlock these lines (whole
 * cache invalidation unlocks), or need to re-lock lines back.
 * Also side effect - half of lines will be cached, half - not.
 * So may need to shuffle data to make hot data cacheable.
 */// #ifdef __GNUC__// #ifndef __ASSEMBLY__// #ifndef __RUBY_MEM_H/*
