 * more flash chips.  This current list focusses on newer chips, which
 * have been converging on command sets which including JEDEC ID.
 *//* Atmel -- some are (confusingly) marketed as "DataFlash" *//* Spansion -- single (large) sector size only, at least
	 * for the chips listed here (without boot sectors).
	 *//* S25FL129P has same jedec_id, but higher frequency - so it should be supported, but at not at maximum speed *//* Micron *//* SST -- large erase sizes are "overlays", "sectors" are 4K *//* ST Microelectronics -- newer production may have feature updates *//* Winbond -- w25x "blocks" are 64K, except w25q128 is 4K  *//* Macronix -- MX25L "blocks" are 64K, except mx25l12836e and mx25l25635 are 4K *//* ESMT -- F25L "blocks are 64K, "sectors" are 4KiB *//* EON -- EN25Q "blocks are 64K, "sectors" are 4KiB *//* GD -- GD25Q "blocks are 64K, "sectors" are 4KiB */// #ifndef __SPI_FLASH_DATA_H/*
