 *//* for ieee80211_nodestats *//* for proto macros on node *//* #define IEEE80211_DEBUG_REFCNT *//*
 * Each ieee80211com instance has a single timer that fires once a
 * second.  This is used to initiate various work depending on the
 * state of the instance: scanning (passive or active), ``transition''
 * (waiting for a response to a management frame when operating
 * as a station), and node inactivity processing (when operating
 * as an AP).  For inactivity processing each node has a timeout
 * set in it's ni_inact field that is decremented on each timeout
 * and the node is reclaimed when the counter goes to zero.  We
 * use different inactivity timeout values depending on whether
 * the node is associated and authorized (either by 802.1x or
 * open/shared key authentication) or associated but yet to be
 * authorized.  The latter timeout is shorter to more aggressively
 * reclaim nodes that leave part way through the 802.1x exchange.
 *//* inactivity interval (secs) *//* initial *//* associated but not authorized *//* authorized *//* probe *//* scanned *//* The threshold that starts to send detection packet *//* mgt frame tx timer (secs) + random32()%HZ *//* simple hash is enough for variation of macaddr *//* mcast/group cipher *//* mcast key length *//* unicast cipher set *//* selected unicast cipher *//* unicast key length *//* key management algorithms *//* selected key mgmt algo *//* capabilities *//* ms *//* ms *//* Radio measurement - STA Statistics *//* ... *//* report mode *//* last receive time *//* wait queue for syncing with user space *//* flag indicating pending request from user space *//* 0 = success; 1 = timeout; 2 = node leave *//* measurement result *//**
 * Local qdrv node statistics for smoothing
 *//*
 * Node specific information.  Note that drivers are expected
 * to derive from this structure to add device-specific per-node
 * state.  This is done by overriding the ic_node_* methods in
 * the ieee80211com structure.
 *//* gen# for timeout scan *//* authentication algorithm *//* special-purpose state *//* extended special-purpose state *//* Atheros feature flags *//* NB: These must have the same values as IEEE80211_ATHC_* *//* Turbo prime enable *//* Compresssion enable *//* Fast Frame capable *//* Atheros WME enable *//* AR capable *//* PS state change *//* Atheros def key index *//* Broadcom feature flags *//* flag to disallow BBF *//* flag to disallow standard BF *//* assoc response *//* local node index *//* current transmit power (in 0.5 dBm) *//* vlan tag *//* shared-key challenge *//* captured WPA ie *//* captured RSN ie *//* captured OSEN ie *//* captured WME ie *//* captured WSC ie *//* captured Atheros ie *//* captured Quantenna ie from assoc *//* captured QTN Pairing IE from assoc *//* captured QTN brmacs IE for TDLS *//* extender role of the node *//* captured extender bssid IE *//* tx seq per-tid *//* rx seq previous per-tid*//* time stamp of last rx frag *//* rx frag reassembly *//* RSN/WPA parameters *//* unicast key *//* Receive key offset *//* parsed HT capabilities *//* received htcap IE *//* parsed HT information *//* received htinfo IE *//* VSP BA throtting bitmap *//* used to calculate traffic per check interval *//* action token *//* Implicit block ack flags as passed in by the client *//* block ack *//* timer for running rate training *//* 11n information *//* recommended tx channel width *//* channel width changed *//* hardware *//* recv timestamp *//* recv jiffies *//* recv ssi *//* Smoothed RSSI *//* conservative index for rate ratio in scs channel ranking *//* Total time (Rx + Tx) *//* rxglitch consecutively exceed threshold *//* header *//* beacon, probe response *//* from last rcv'd beacon *//* raw beacon interval *//* beacon interval *//* beacon interval before first change *//* count of ni_intval != ni_intval_old *//* end of transition interval jiffies *//* TBTT of AP node *//* dtim TBTT of AP node *//* capabilities *//* negotiated rate set *//* negotiated ht rate set *//* supported channels bitmap *//* supported channels number *//* FH only *//* FH only *//* ERP from beacon/probe resp *//* byte offset to TIM ie *//* action frame, radio measurement category, sta statistics *//* others *//* packets queued for pspoll *//* inactivity mark count *//* inactivity reload value *//* inactivity workqueue *//* index to ni_rates[] *//* per-node statistics *//* previously associated vap *//* U-APSD per-node flags matching WMM STA Qos Info field *//* trigger suppression on retry *//* link quality - provisional - currently TX PHY rate*//* MAC filtering timeout in jiffies - 0 if not blacklisted*//* Support 4-addr encap of LNCB packets (multicast) *//* List of STAs supporting 4 address LNCB packets *//* List of bridge STAs *//* start time of association (jiffies) *//* 802.11k related *//* TPC related *//* Measurement related *//* mainly for measurement report *//* IPv6 link local address *//* For TDLS path selection *//* jiffies TDLS peer is last seen *//* Last path selection result *//* Continuous same path selection number*//* tdls peer node's AID, allocated by AP, unique value at BSS *//* TDLS status *//* TDLS channel switch request has sent out *//* TDLS peer as initiator *//* TDLS channel switch response not send yet*//* jiffies TDLS setup start *//* These values must be kept in sync with ieee80211_node_type_str *//*
 * Association IDs are managed with a bit vector.
 *//*Will expand the bitmap to include other power save schemes*//* 10 minutes *//*
 * Table of ieee80211_node instances.  Each ieee80211com
 * has at least one for holding the scan candidates.
 * When operating as an access point or in ibss mode there
 * is a second table for associated stations or neighbors.
 *//* back reference *//* on node table *//* information of all nodes *//* for debugging *//* on nt_scangen *//* gen# for timeout scan *//* initial node inact setting *//* timer to age out wds entries *//* IEEE80211_DEBUG_REFCNT *//* IEEE80211_DEBUG_REFCNT *//*
 * Set up the implicit block ACK for the given node.
 * ni the node to set up the implicit BA agreement with. The bitmap of TIDs is within the
 * ni_implicit_ba field of the ieee80211_node structure.
 *//* _NET80211_IEEE80211_NODE_H_ *//*-
