 for STA power-saving *//* Quantenna flags from bcn/probe resp (station only) *//* Quantenna capability flags *//* 1 - is QTN dev, 0 - is not QTN dev *//* new state parameters for tasklet for stajoin1 *//* tasklet for newstate action called from stajoin1tq *//* node_idx to use for tx of non specifically targetted frames *//* Logical group assigned for SSID, used for BSS association limits *//* IWSPY support *//* Done with scheduled newstate tasklet *//* state machine state *//* MCS configuration for 11N and 11AC or -1 for autorate *//* HT mode mandatory flags *//* VHT mode htcap flags *//* is dsss/cck OKAY in 40MHz? *//* is non GF STA present? (always 1 for 88K) *//* atleast one 20 MHz STA in 20/40 MHz BSS found *//* HT Non-HT mixed mode is desired *//* HT dual CTS protection is required *//* is lsig in TXOP ok *//* is current beacon a stbc beacon *//* The overridden value for SMPS for the STA. *//* Implicit block ack flags for the VAP. *//* Block ack control - zero indicates accept no BAs,
							   bit in position 'n' indicates accept and send BA for the given TID *//* Old block ack control *//* MAC Filtering *//* Maximum window size allowable *//* Rate training to new STAs - number of bursts *//* Rate training to new STAs - packets per burst *//* Multicast legacy rates *//* Forward packets even if we have no bridge entry for them *//* Forward mcast/bcast as unicast *//* For WFA testing only *//* pairing pending queue *//* count of disconnection event *//* sequence to query disconnection count *//* timer to start xr *//* Interval of periodically sending NULL packet to all associated STAs. 0 means disable *//* Enable/disable 11AC feature on Topaz *//* vap priority, used to calculate priority for per node per tid queue *//* VAP PMF/802.11w capability options *//* local max transmit power, equal to regulatory max power minus power constraint *//* Per-VAP WME/WMM state for AP mode *//* Enable/disable A-MSDU  *//* Max TX A-MSDU *//* 802.11u related *//* 1 - Enabled, 0 - Disabled *//* Interworking information *//* Enable/Disable HS2.0 *//* Disable Downstream Group-Addressed Forwarding - used by HS2.0 *//* 1 - Enabled,  0- Disabled *//* 1 - TKIP is allowed, 0 - TKIP is not allowed *//* 1 - block, 0 - unblock *//* 1 - TXBA disable, 0 - TXBA permitted *//* 1 - RXBA decline, 0 - RXBA permitted *//* 1 - enabled, 0 - disabled *//* 1/0 - OSEN enabled/disabled *//* 1 - IEEE80211_AC_ONLY, 2 - IEEE80211_N_ONLY *//* step to next channel *//* first channel in the band *//* channels in the band *//*
 * Note: A node table lock must be acquired or IRQ disabled to maintain atomic
 * when calling this function, and must not be released until a node ref is taken
