 *//*
 * 802.11 protocol definitions.
 *//* size of 802.11 address *//* is 802.11 address multicast/broadcast? *//* IEEE 802.11 PLCP header *//*
 * generic definitions for IEEE 802.11 frames
 *//* possibly followed by addr4[IEEE80211_ADDR_LEN]; *//* see below *//* possibly followed by addr4[IEEE80211_ADDR_LEN]; *//* see below *//* possibly followed by addr4[IEEE80211_ADDR_LEN]; *//* see below *//* possibly followed by addr4[IEEE80211_ADDR_LEN]; *//* see below *//* AID or duration *//* for TYPE_MGT *//* for TYPE_CTL *//* for TYPE_DATA (bit combination) *//* STA->STA *//* STA->AP  *//* AP ->STA *//* AP ->AP  *//* bit 8 is reserved *//* bit 1 is reserved *//* bits 4-5 are reserved *//* bits 1-5 are reserved *//*
 * Country/Region Codes from MS WINNLS.H
 * Numbering from ISO 3166
 * XXX belongs elsewhere
 *
 * First 2 entries taken from ieee80211.c ...
 *//* debug, = 511 radix 10 *//* default or not defined *//* Afghanistan *//* Albania *//* Algeria *//* American Samoa *//* Andorra *//* Angola *//* Antartica *//* Antigua and Barbuda *//* Argentina *//* Armenia *//* Aruba *//* Australia *//* Austria *//* Azerbaijan *//* Bahamas *//* Bahrain *//* Bangladesh *//* Belarus *//* Belgium *//* Belize *//* Bolivia *//* Brazil *//* Brunei Darussalam *//* Bulgaria *//* Canada *//* Chile *//* People's Republic of China *//* Colombia *//* Costa Rica *//* Croatia *//* Czech Republic *//* Denmark *//* Dominican Republic *//* Ecuador *//* European Union *//* Egypt *//* El Salvador *//* Estonia *//* (Malvinas) *//* Faeroe Islands *//* Finland *//* France *//* France2 *//* Georgia *//* Germany *//* Greece *//* Guatemala *//* Honduras *//* Hong Kong S.A.R., P.R.C. *//* Hungary *//* Iceland *//* India *//* Indonesia *//* Iran *//* Iraq *//* Ireland *//* Israel *//* Italy *//* Jamaica *//* Japan *//* Japan (JP1) *//* Japan (JP0) *//* Japan (JP1-1) *//* Japan (JE1) *//* Japan (JE2) *//* Japan (JP6) *//* Japan *//* Japan *//* Japan *//* Japan *//* Japan *//* Japan *//* Japan *//* Japan *//* Japan *//* Japan *//* Japan *//* Japan *//* Japan *//* Japan *//* Japan *//* Japan *//* Japan *//* Japan *//* Japan *//* Japan *//* Japan *//* Japan *//* Japan *//* Japan *//* Japan *//* Japan *//* Japan *//* Japan *//* Japan *//* Japan *//* Japan *//* Japan *//* Japan *//* Japan *//* Japan *//* Japan *//* Japan *//* Japan *//* Japan *//* Japan *//* Japan *//* Japan *//* Jordan *//* Kazakhstan *//* Kenya *//* North Korea *//* South Korea *//* South Korea *//* Kuwait *//* Latvia *//* Lebanon *//* Libya *//* Liechtenstein *//* Lithuania *//* Luxembourg *//* Macau *//* the Former Yugoslav Republic of Macedonia *//* Malaysia *//* Mexico *//* Principality of Monaco *//* Morocco *//* Nepal *//* Netherlands *//* New Zealand *//* Nicaragua *//* Norway *//* Oman *//* Islamic Republic of Pakistan *//* Panama *//* Paraguay *//* Peru *//* Republic of the Philippines *//* Poland *//* Portugal *//* Puerto Rico *//* Qatar *//* Romania *//* Russia *//* Saudi Arabia *//* Singapore *//* Slovak Republic *//* Slovenia *//* South Africa *//* Spain *//* Sri Lanka *//* Sweden *//* Switzerland *//* Syria *//* Taiwan *//* Thailand *//* Trinidad y Tobago *//* Tunisia *//* Turkey *//* U.A.E. *//* Ukraine *//* United Kingdom *//* United States *//* United States (Public Safety)*//* Uruguay *//* Uzbekistan *//* Venezuela *//* Viet Nam *//* Yemen *//* Zimbabwe *//*
 * Generic information element
 *//*
 * Country information element.
 *//*
 * Channel Switch Announcement information element.
 *//* IEEE80211_ELEMID_CHANSWITCHANN *//* == 3 *//* Channel Switch Mode: 1 == stop transmission until CS *//* New Channel Number *//* TBTTs until Channel Switch happens *//* for Spectrum Management Actions. Table 20e in 802.11h $7.4.1 *//* for csa_mode. It must be either 0 or 1. 1 means that the receiver shall stop
 * sending until CS. 0 imposes no requirement. See 7.3.2.20 *//* minimal Channel Switch Count in the initial announcement *//* maximum allowed deviance of measurement of intervals between CSA in Beacons *//* Quantenna CSA tsf ie, to complement an 802.11h CSA ie. More timing precision *//* IEEE80211_ELEMID_VENDOR *//* length in bytes *//* QTN_OUI - 0x00, 0x26, 0x86*//* IE type *//* TSF at which channel change happens. *//* Quantenna SCS IE *//* IEEE80211_ELEMID_VENDOR *//* length in bytes *//* QTN_OUI - 0x00, 0x26, 0x86*//* IE type *//* for future expansion and backward compatibility *//* following depends on scs_ie_type *//* short preamble failure in last second *//* long preamble failure in last second *//* rx + tx time for all nodes *//* extra ie len *//* tdls stats *//* till scs ie type *//* does frame have QoS sequence control data *//* Mask for Param Set Count field *//*
 * WME/802.11e information element.
 *//* IEEE80211_ELEMID_VENDOR *//* length in bytes *//* 0x00, 0x50, 0xf2 *//* OUI type *//* OUI subtype *//* spec revision *//* QoS info *//*
 * WME/802.11e Tspec Element
 *//*
 * WME AC parameter field
 *//* 16 tids *//* 4 AC categories *//* Mask for ACI field *//* Shift for ACI field *//* Mask for ACM bit *//* Shift for ACM bit *//* Mask for aifsn field *//* Shift for aifsn field *//* Mask for CwMin field (in log) *//* Shift for CwMin field *//* Mask for CwMax field (in log) *//* Shift for CwMax field *//*
 * WME Parameter Element
 *//*
 * WME U-APSD qos info field defines
 *//* byte 0 *//* byte 7 *//*
 * 20/40 MHZ BSS coexistence information element.
 *//*
 * 20/40 MHZ BSS intolerant channel report information element.
 *//*
 * Overlapping BSS Scan Parameter information element.
 *//*
 * Atheros Advanced Capability information element.
 *//* IEEE80211_ELEMID_VENDOR *//* length in bytes *//* 0x00, 0x03, 0x7f *//* OUI type *//* OUI subtype *//* spec revision *//* Capability info *//*
 * Atheros XR information element.
 *//* Atheros capabilities *//* Turbo Prime *//* Compression *//* Fast Frames *//* Xtended Range support *//* Advanced Radar support *//* Bursting - not negotiated *//* CWMin tuning *//* Boost *//*
 * Quantenna Flags information element.
 * Fields up to qtn_ie_implicit_ba_tid are backwards-compatible with Envy images.
 *//* IEEE80211_ELEMID_VENDOR *//* length in bytes *//* QTN_OUI - 0x00, 0x26, 0x86 *//* IE type *//* See below *//* V2 fields *//* Implicit block ACKs, set up directly after assoc *//* See below *//* V3 fields *//* Implicit block ACK with variable size - overrides v2 implicit BA field. *//* Size of implicit BA >> 2 *//* V4 fields *//* VSP version *//* V5 fields *//*
 * Quantenna WME information element.
 *//* IEEE80211_ELEMID_VENDOR *//* length in bytes *//* QTN_OUI - 0x00, 0x26, 0x86*//* IE type *//*
 * QTN Pairing TLV element.
 *  Format:
 *   Type(1byte)   |   len(2bytes)    |  SHA-256 hash(32bytes)
 *      0x1        |        35        |     SHA-256 hash material of pairing
 *//*
 * QTN Pairing IE
 *  Format:
 *  IE ID(1byte)    |     IE len(1byte)    |     IE OUI(3bytes)    | IE content(pairing)
 *     0xdd         |       38             |        00 26 86       |     Pairing TLV
 *
 *//* Disable Station side control for QTM-Lite *//* not CONFIG_QVSP *//* CONFIG_QVSP *//*
 * These flags are used in the following two fields.
 * - qtn_ie_flags contains the sender's settings, except in an association response, where
 *   it contains confirmation of the settings received from the peer station.  These flags
 *   must remain backwards-compatible with Envy images.
 * - qtn_ie_my_flags always contains the sender's settings.  It is not sent by Envy systems.
 *//* Use 4-addr headers *//* Envy beamforming *//* Ruby 2 stream beamforming *//* Multicast packets in the local network
							 * control block are 4 address encapsulated.
							 *//* Ruby 4 stream non-standard beamforming *//* Envy with 'my flags' field in the IE. *//* 4 strm standard bf with tone grouping *//* Ruby TX AMSDU *//* Quantenna TDLS Discovery Response clients information element *//* IEEE80211_ELEMID_VENDOR *//* 0x00, 0x26, 0x86 *//* IEEE_QTN_IE_TYPE_TDLS_CLIENTS *//* Number of downstream MAC addresses *//* Start of downstream MAC addresses *//*
 * Management Notification Frame
 *//*
 * Management Action Frames
