 * 802.11n HT Capability IE
 *//* element ID *//* length in bytes *//* HT capabilities *//* A-MPDU parameters *//* supported MCS set *//* extended HT capabilities *//* txbf capabilities *//* antenna capabilities *//* HT capability flags *//* 1 = 8K, 0 = 3839 bytes *//* STBC defines *//* MCS set flags *//* Maximum MSDU sizes *//* Extended capabilities flags *//* Tx Beamforming flags *//* Antenna selection flags *//* 11 AC related defines *//* B0-1 maximum rx A-MPDU factor 2^(13+Max Rx A-MPDU Factor) - 1 *//* (2 ^ 13) - 1*//* (2 ^ 14) - 1 *//* (2 ^ 15) - 1*//* (2 ^ 16) - 1*//* B2-4 MPDU spacing (usec) *//* No time restriction *//* 1/4 usec *//* 1/2 usec *//* 1 usec *//* 2 usec *//* 4 usec *//* 8 usec *//* 16 usec *//*
 * Rx MCS set
 * # Supported rates IE is a 10 octet bitmap - also see mcs_stream_map[]
 * Octet: 0        1        2        3        4 UEQM1  5 UEQM2  6 UEQM3  7 UEQM4  8 UEQM5  9 UEQM6
 * NSS:   11111111 22222222 33333333 44444444 02222223 33333333 33333444 44444444 44444444 44444...
 * MCS:   0        8        16       24       32       40       48       56       64       72  76
 *//* CBW = 20/40 MHz, Nss = 1, Nes = 1, EQM/ No EQM *//* CBW = 20/40 MHz, Nss = 2, Nes = 1, EQM *//* CBW = 20/40 MHz, Nss = 3, Nes = 1, EQM *//* CBW = 20/40 MHz, Nss = 4, Nes = 1, EQM *//* MCS 32 and UEQM MCSs 33 - 39 *//* UEQM MCSs 40 - 47 *//* UEQM MCSs 48 - 55 *//* UEQM MCSs 56 - 63 *//* UEQM MCSs 64 - 71 *//* UEQM MCSs 72 - 76 plus 3 reserved bits *//* B2-3 Maximum Tx spatial streams *//* One spatial stream *//* Two spatial streams *//* Three spatial streams *//* Four spatial streams *//* B2-3 power save mode *//* No MIMO (static mode) *//* Precede MIMO with RTS *//* Not applicable        *//* No limitation on MIMO (SM power save disabled) *//* B8-9 Rx STBC Mode *//* No STBC SS *//* One STBC SS *//* Two STBC SS *//* Three STBC SS *//* B1-2 PCO transition time *//* No transition *//* 400 us *//* 1.5 ms *//* 5 ms *//* B8-9 MCS feedback *//* No feedback *//* Reserved *//* Unsolicited feedback only*//* Solicited and unsolicited feedback *//* B6-7 Calibration *//* No support *//* Response only *//* Reserved *//* Request and response *//* B11-12 explicit CSI TxBF feedback, B13-14 explicit non compressed TxBF,
 * B15-16 explicit compressed TxBF
 *//* No support *//* delayed response only *//* immediate response only *//* both delayed and immediate response *//* B17-18 Grouping *//* No support *//* groups 1 and 2 *//* groups 1 and 4 *//* groups 1, 2 and 4 *//* B19-20 CSI number of beamforming antennas, B21-22 non compressed number of beamforming
 * antennas, B23-24 compressed number of beamforming antennas
 *//* Single antenna sounding *//* 2 antenna sounding *//* 3 antenna sounding *//* 4 antenna sounding *//* B25-26 CSI Max number of beamformer rows *//* B27-28 channel estimation capability *//* one space time stream *//* two space time streams *//* three space time streams *//* four space time streams *//* HT NSS *//* HT capability macros *//* get macros *//* A-MPDU spacing  B2-B4 *//* max RX A-MPDU length  B0-B1 *//* highest supported data rate, B0-B7 in set 10, B0-B1 in set 11 *//* MCS parameters (all bits)*//* MCS maximum spatial streams, B2-B3 in set 12 *//* MCS set value (all bits) *//* HT capabilities (all bits) *//* B3-4 power save mode *//* B8-9 Rx STBC MODE *//* HT extended capabilities (all bits) *//* B1-2 PCO transition time *//* B8-9 MCS feedback type *//* HT TxBeamForming (bits 0-13) *//* HT TxBeamForming (bits 14-31) *//* B6-7 Calibration *//* B11-12 explicit CSI TxBF feedback*//* B13-14 explicit non compressed TxBF *//* B15-16 explicit compressed TxBF *//* B17-18 Grouping *//* B19-20 CSI number of beamforming antennas *//* B21-22 non compressed number of beamforming antennas *//* B23-24 compressed number of beamforming antennas *//* B25-26 CSI Max number of beamformer rows *//* B27-28 channel estimation capability *//* set macros *//* A-MPDU spacing  B2-B4 *//* max RX A-MPDU length  B0-B1 *//* highest supported data rate, B0-B7 in set 10, B0-B1 in set 11) *//* MCS set parameters (all bits) *//* MCS maximum spatial streams, B2-B3 in set 12 *//* MCS set value (all bits) *//* HT capabilities (all bits) *//* B2-B3 power save mode *//* B8-9 Rx STBC MODE *//* HT extended capabilities (all bits) *//* B1-2 PCO transition time *//* B8-9 MCS feedback type *//* HT TxBeamForming (all bits ) *//* B6-7 Calibration *//* B11-12 explicit CSI TxBF feedback*//* B13-14 explicit non compressed TxBF *//* B15-16 explicit compressed TxBF *//* B17-18 Grouping *//* B19-20 CSI number of beamforming antennas *//* B21-22 non compressed number of beamforming antennas *//* B23-24 compressed number of beamforming antennas *//* B25-26 CSI Max number of beamformer rows *//* B27-28 channel estimation capability *//*
 * 802.11n HT Information IE
 *//* element ID *//* length in bytes *//* control channel *//* ht ie byte 1 *//* ht ie byte 2 *//* ht ie byte 3 *//* ht ie byte 4 *//* ht ie byte 5 *//* basic MCS set *//* get macros *//* control channel (all bits) *//* byte 1 (all bits) *//* byte 2 (all bits) *//* byte 3 (all bits) *//* byte 4 (all bits) *//* byte 5 (all bits) *//* B5-B7, byte 1 *//* B0-B1, byte 1 *//* B0-B1, byte 2 *//* MCS set value (all bits) *//* set macros *//* control channel (all bits) *//* byte 1 (all bits) *//* byte 2 (all bits) *//* byte 3 (all bits) *//* byte 4 (all bits) *//* byte 5 (all bits) *//* B5-B7, byte 1 *//* B0-B1, byte 1 *//* B0-B1, byte 2 *//* Basic MCS set value (all bits) *//* extension channel offset (2 bit signed number) *//* 0  no extension channel is present *//* +1 extension channel above control channel *//* -2 undefined *//* -1 extension channel below control channel*//* operating mode *//* no protection *//* protection required (Legacy device present in other BSS) *//* protection required ( One 20 MHZ only HT device is present in 20/40 BSS) *//* protection required (Legacy device is present in this BSS) *//* signal granularity *//* 5 ms *//* 10 ms *//* 15 ms *//* 20 ms *//* 25 ms *//* 30 ms *//* 35 ms *//* 40 ms *//*
 * Management information element payloads.
 *//* 17-31 reserved for challenge text extension *//* Secondary Channel Offset *//* 20/40 BSS Coexistence *//* 20/40 BSS Intolerant channel report *//* Overlapping BSS scan parameter  *//* TDLS Link Identifier *//* TDLS Wakeup Schedule *//* TDLS Channel Switch Timing *//* TDLS PTI Control *//* TDLS PU Buffer Status *//* 128-129 proprietary elements used by Agere chipsets *//* 191-199 Table 8-54-Element IDs in Std 802.11ac-2013 *//* Vendor Specific *//* vendor private *//* Notify Channel Width Action size *//* MU grp id mgmt action size *//*
