 *//*
 * IEEE 802.11 ioctls.
 *//*
 * Per-channel flags to differentiate chan_pri_inactive configuration
 * between regulatory db and user configuration.
 * By default, system uses static regulatory db configs.
 * However driver shall always honour dynamic user coniguration.
 * In this way, user configuration will override regulatory db configs.
 *//*
 * Per/node (station) statistics available when operating as an AP.
 *//* rx data frames *//* rx management frames *//* rx control frames *//* rx unicast frames *//* rx multicast frames *//* rx broadcast frames *//* rx data count (bytes) *//* rx beacon frames *//* rx probe response frames *//* rx discard because it's a dup *//* rx w/ wep but privacy off *//* rx wep processing failed *//* rx demic failed *//* rx decapsulation failed *//* rx defragmentation failed *//* rx disassociation *//* rx deauthentication *//* rx decrypt failed on crc *//* rx on unauthorized port *//* rx unecrypted w/ privacy *//* tx data frames *//* tx management frames *//* tx unicast frames *//* tx multicast frames *//* tx broadcast frames *//* tx data count (bytes) *//* tx probe request frames *//* tx on uapsd queue *//* tx discard due to no tag *//* tx discard due to of bad tag *//* rx on unauthorized port *//* uapsd EOSP retried out *//* ps discard due to of age *//* uapsd triggers *//* MIB-related state *//* [re]associations *//* [re]association failures *//* [re]authentications *//* [re]authentication failures*//* deauthentications *//* last deauth reason *//* disassociations *//* last disassociation reason *//* power save queue drops *//* rx action *//*
