 **//*
 * Define EP state during host suspend
 * 0 = EP does not power off
 * 1 = EP power off
 *//* Quantenna PCIE vendor and device identifiers  *//* Clear endian flags *//* Get EP Mapping address *//* Reset DMA offset in bda *//* Request compressed firmware from user space *//*
		 * No firmware found in the firmware directory, skip firmware downloading process
		 * boot from flash directly on target
		 *//* Start loading firmware *//* flush dcache *//* Mark end of block *//*
	* Set Max_Payload_Size
	* Max_Payload_Size_in_effect = 1 << ( ( (dev_ctl >> 5) & 0x07) + 7);
	*//* When system boots up, the state of pdev is not saved on the entry of this function.
	 * Data structure pci_dev will keep in use when module is removed and re-installed.
	 * So we can call pci_restore_sate() to recover its previous configuration space.
	 *//* Save "fresh poweron" state including BAR address, etc. So the state can be
	 * used for recovery next time.
	 *//* Allocate device structure *//* allocate netlink data buffer *//* Check if the device has PCI express capability *//*  Wake up the device if it is in suspended state and allocate IO,
	 *  memory regions and IRQ if not
	 *//*
	 * Check if the PCI device can support DMA addressing properly.
	 * The mask gives the bits that the device can address
	 *//* Initialize PCIE layer  *//* Create and start the thread to initiate the INIT Handshake*//* Create netlink & register with kernel *//* Releasing the memory region if any error occured *//* Any failure in probe, so it can directly return in remove *//* Set ep not ready to drop packets in low power mode *//* Set ep_ready to resume tx traffic *//*  Register the pci driver with device*//* Release netlink *//* Unregister the pci driver with the device *//* Wait EP link up. If this function is called at hardirq context where 10s
	 * delay is not allowed, please replace with link up check at Root Complex's
	 * status register.
         *//* Re-allocate and initialize data structure *//* Read PCIe configuration space header *//* Endian value will be all 1s if link went down *//* Check if reset to EP occurred *//* Save target-side MSI address for later enable/disable irq*//* Parsing the netlink message *//*
	 * make new skbs; Fragment if necessary.
	 * The original skb will be freed in netlink_unicast_kernel,
	 * we hold the new skbs until DMA transfer is done
	 *//**
