 **//*  Initialize interrupts *//* Memory Initialization *//* Set default to use Legacy INTx interrupt *//* Check if the device has MSI capability *//* NOTE:
		  * Do not use an implicit length such as the BAR length
		  * if the map length is too large say > 16Mb this leaves
		  * the implementation vulnerable to
		  * Linux and the attack of the Silent  "S" (one between the n and u)
		  *//*initialized BAR *//* Check the span of the BAR including the offset + length, bar_end points to the last byte of BAR *//* Unitialized bar *//* Checks that offset area is within bar *//* Checks that mapped area is within bar *//* Reserve PCIe memory region*//* Map SynControl registers and Host to Endpoint interrupt registers to BAR-2 *//* Reserve PCIe memory region*//**
