 **//* For cache line size definitions *//* For cache flushing functions *//* Tx dump flag *//* vmac s 32 *//* vmac s 33 *//* Rx dump flag *//* vmac s 48 *//* vmac s 49 *//* vmac s 50 *//* Alignment helper functions *//* Print the Tx Request Queue *//* Print Tx Rquest Queue *//* show Rx BD *//* show vmac interrupt statistic info *//* disable all of runtime dump *//* used for vmac_dbg_show *//* used for runtime dump *//* enable all of runtime dump *//* dev_attr_dbg *//* dev_attr_pmctrl *//* Length of allocated Transmitted & Received descriptor array *//* uint32_t is used to be updated by ep *//* Update pointers related with Tx descriptor table *//* Update pointers related with Rx descriptor table *//* Update pointers used by EP's updating consumed packet index *//* check for undersize skb; this should never happen, and indicates problems elsewhere *//* Move skb->data to a cache line boundary *//* QTN_SKB_RECYCLE_SUPPORT *//* last fragment -- hand it to upper layer *//*
 * TODO: vmac_irq_napi_fixup needs to undergo stability and
 * especially performance test to justify its value
*//*
 * skb buffer have a pading, so skb data move less than pading is safe
 *
 *//*bytes_boundary == 0 means etherheader is 4 byte aligned,
	 *so IP header is 2(+14 ether header) byte aligned,
	 *move whole packet 2 byte ahead for QCA NSS preference
	*//* Double Check if it's netlink packet*//* QTN_SKB_RECYCLE_SUPPORT *//*
		 * We are done with the current buffer attached to this descriptor, so attach a new
		 * one.
		 *//* prevent old packet from passing the packet up *//* prevent old packet from passing the packet up *//* QTN_SKB_RECYCLE_SUPPORT *//* Move skb->data to a cache line boundary *//* QTN_SKB_RECYCLE_SUPPORT *//* Invalidate cache and map virtual address to bus address. *//* TODO: packet length, currently don't check the length *//* QTN_SKB_RECYCLE_SUPPORT *//* tbd index *//* Tx BD pointer *//* TODO: Under current architect, register_netdev() is called
	before EP is ready. So an variable ep_ready is added to achieve
	defensive programming. We need to change the code segment later *//* Tear down the previous skb transmitted by DMA *//* Reserve one entry space to differentiate full and empty case *//* Update local descriptor array *//* Update remote Request Queue *//* Deassert remote INTx message *//*
 * The Tx ring has been full longer than the watchdog timeout
 * value. The transmitter must be hung?
 *//* ethtools support *//* Allocate device structure *//* Initialize private data *//* Allocate Tx & Rx SKB descriptor array *//* Allocate and initialise Tx & Rx descriptor array *//* Initialize NAPI *//* Register device *//* Add the device attributes *//* All Ethernet activity should have ceased before calling
	 * this function
	 *//* All Ethernet activity should have ceased before calling
	 * this function
	 *//* Allocate rx buffers *//* Interface will be ready to send/receive data, but will need hooking
	 * up to the interrupts before anything will happen.
	 *//* Close down MAC and DMA activity and clear all data. *//* Todo: request_irq here *//**
