 **/// registers 0-12 are caller saves, 13-25 callee saves, gp, fp, sp/* fit 4k (1024 * 32bit) of aligned values, 4k of unaligned, and a tiny pad *//* look through the memory at and address +- 16b *//* N.B. this printk itself triggers unaligned accesses *//* check for differences in the registers, caused by either the load or by register write back.
   put the results as sprintfs into 'buf'. returns the number of bytes written into 'buf', i.e. 0 = nothing to report *//* register stores, to observe difference in register state before and after instructions *//* fill registers with values to set up a test, then execute for both val1a and val1b 
   which are typically 2 memory areas, 1 for aligned and 1 for unaligned data */// one of each permutation of each instruction, as found in a kernel objdump// .di instructions are not handled by the routine, they cause a sigsegv//CHECK(r3, "ld.a.di	r8,[r3,4]\n"::);//CHECK(r3, "ld.di	r2,[r3,8]\n"::);//CHECK(r3, "ldw.ab.di	r8,[r3,12]\n"::);//CHECK(r3, "ldw.a.di	r8,[r3,16]\n"::);//CHECK(r3, "ldw.as.di	r8,[r3,20]\n"::);//CHECK(r3, "ldw.di	r2,[r3,24]\n"::);//CHECK(r3, "ldw.x.ab.di	r4,[r3,-184]\n"::);//CHECK(r3, "st.di	r2,[r3,-24]\n"::);// higher registers// altering sp and fp crash the test harness (make sense...). compiler doesn't like gp being clobbered//CHECK(sp,  r2, "ld.a	r2,[sp,8]\n"::);//CHECK(fp,  r5, "ld.ab	r5,[fp,4]\n"::);//CHECK(gp,  r2, "ld.as	r2,[gp,92]\n"::);//CHECK(sp,  r2, "ldw.a	r2,[sp,-2]\n"::);//CHECK(gp,  r5, "ldw.ab	r5,[gp,2]\n"::);//CHECK(fp,  r2, "ldw.as	r2,[fp,161]\n"::);//CHECK(sp, r6, "stw.a	r6,[sp,-6]\n"::);//CHECK(gp, r5, "stw.ab	r5,[gp,6]\n"::);//CHECK(fp, r2, "stw.as	r2,[fp,-10]\n"::);/* copy an int to a buffer at arbitrary offset, using byte operations to avoid faulting */// little endian// the first half of the buffer will be aligned values// second half will be unaligned, same stuff but 1kb+1b offset// 2k of offset in either direction// __UNALIGNED_ACCESS_H/*-
