	 *//* Currently we don't support BRCM 11AC STA's CC request*//* reset entry *//* always scale cca_intf so that it is adaptive to cca duration change and off-chan sample *//* current channel's cca_intf use maximum of AP and STAs *//* update off-channel sampling stats with exponential smoothing *//* only have AP side off-channel sampling now *//* only have AP side off-channel sampling now *//* let sta side pmbl smoothing out *//* mark channel entry updated so it won't be aged out *//*
 * This function should NOT be called right after the txpower change because the rssi may come
 * from the original txpower. Make sure txpower and rssi is match.
 *//* get recent and smooth *//* exponential smooth *//* report smoothed one to ranking database *//* clear the attenuation summary stats before collecting from nodes *//* let all node update their own information into the ranking stats database *//* ms *//* ms *//* ms *//* ms *//* ms *//* ms *//* Add some compensation because (tx_time+rx_time) always is less than the caused cca interference *//* if only downstream traffic or no traffic, don't add compensation *//*  calculate compensation *//* get other nodes' tx/rx time and smooth them *//* old smooth value *//* smooth cca interference *//*
		 * Add some compansation since training packets could
		 * cause high interference in bad environment
