EH1*//* 239.255.255.250 *//* 224.0.0.0/4 *//* ff00::/8 - see __ipv6_addr_type() *//* 224.0.0.0/24 *//*
 * IPv6 broadcasts are scoped multicast.
 * +--------+----+----+---------------------------------------------+
 * | 8      | 4  | 4  |                 112 bits                    |
 * +------ -+----+----+---------------------------------------------+
 * |11111111|flgs|scop|                 group ID                    |
 * +--------+----+----+---------------------------------------------+
 *
 *  Scope:
 *  1: Interface-Local (loopback)
 *  2: Link-Local
 *  4: Admin-Local
 *  5: Site-Local
 *  8: Organization-Local
 *  E: Global
 *  0,3,F: reserved
 *  others: unassigned, are available for administrators to define additional multicast regions.
 *
 *  RFC4291 http://www.iana.org/assignments/ipv6-multicast-addresses/ipv6-multicast-addresses.xml
 *//*
 * IPv6 SSDP is 0xff0?::c
 *//*
 * IPv6 all-nodes multicast address
 * the link-local scope address to reach all nodes is 0xff02::1
 *//* Check for a local network control block MAC address *//*
	 * This is the base IPv6 header. If the next header is an option header, its length must be
	 * accounted for explicitly elsewhere.
	 *//* Multicast data traffic, with the most common types of non-streaming mc filtered out *//*
 * Copyright (c) 2011 Quantenna Communications, Inc.
 *//*
 * This file contains host definitions which are common between the
 * host driver and the microcontroller/MAC code.
 *//* packed definitions for each compiler */// #if defined(MUC_BUILD) || defined(DSP_BUILD) || defined(AUC_BUILD)/* make sure no tids using same index *//* free airtime *//* interference *//**
 * \brief This enumeration represents the mode in use on the device.
 *
 * This enumeration is used to set the correct bandwidth.
 *//* Host tx descriptor *//* Descriptor version *//* packet tid *//* Transmit status: 1 sent to MuC, 2 tx success *//* Reserved for WMM AC*//* Pkt len (incl. all headers) *//* local node index *//* Segment lenghts *//* Phys addr of each seg *//* Timestamp of the pkt *//* Phys addr of next host tx descr in fwd dir *//* Phys addr of next host tx descr in rev dir *//* Virtual addr (LHOST view) of next host tx descr in rev dir *//* Physical addr of this host tx descr *//* Virtual addr (LHOST view) of this host tx descr *//* Status of HTxD *//* MuC callback after txdone *//* parameter for hd_muc_txdone_cb *//* parameter for hd_muc_txdone_cb *//* record the tsf_lo on that frame was sent successfully *//* Can be used for AMSDU destination (append to) *//* Can be used for AMSDU (copy from) *//* Don't update NAV for this frame *//* Don't retry this frame if tx failed *//* Don't return txdesc from MuC to lhost *//* Immediately return txdesc from Muc to lhost *//* host_ioctl_hifinfo *//* Number of ioctl q's *//*
 * LHost -> MuC TX queues are per node to allow variable backpressure per node.
 * One universal management data frame tx mailbox, and one ioctl mailbox
 *//* Start address for mbox *//* IRQ map for rx done *//* IRQ map for tx done *//* Rx FIFO location *//* IRQ map for Scan *//* Scan FIFO location *//* node_idx of the vap node for tx *//* Device name *//* basic firmware version *//* calibration algorithm version *//* Mapping of semaphores *//* need to be aligned on 8 bytes *//* Where the frame was from *//* Pointer to first descriptor in linked list *//* Num elems on fifo *//* Size of fifo *//* the ptr to the host_rxdesc linked list  ready for indication *//* Pointer to request mailbox *//* Pointer to result mailbox *//* Semaphore for Scan fifo *//* Semaphore for Scan fifo *//* Data Descriptor fifo *//* Semaphore for rx fifo *//* Device to run IOCTL on *//* Command type *//* Single valued arg 1 *//* Single valued arg 2 *//* Argument payload pointer *//* Status from other side *//* Command return code *//* link to next msg in chain *//* Create a vap *//* Bring the device up *//* Start Beacon *//* New associated node *//* New associated node *//* Send NDP announcement *//* Configure Parameters *//* Configure Parameters *//* Send the cal cmd *//* General commands *//* Configure node *//* MIMO power save mode change *//* transmission control (turning on or off) *//* Stop transmitting beacons *//* Delete a vap *//* Store the Tx power, short-range workaround*//* Enable-disable RTS-CTS *//* send request to MuC to change power save level *//* Configure QVSP *//* set 11bg ERP on/off *//* notify MUC to execute measurement *//* get rssi info *//* set tdls related paramters *//* set tdls related paramters *//* enter/leave power save state *//* Remain on target channel *//* get MU groups other releated data *//* Set RX gain params *//* get MU enable flag *//* get MU precode enable flag *//* get EQ enable flag *//* Set MuC power table *//* Set Global Vlan mode *//* Update node information again after association *//* control node tx airtime accumulation start|stop *//* suspend/resume all off-channel mechanisms globally *//* Update MU groups: nodes and qmats *//* periodically flush data *//* get the TX max msdu size *//* Dump MuC memory *//* Configuration for dumping MuC memory *//* Configuration for dumping MuC nodes *//* Set MUC debug message level*//* Get MUC debug message level*//* Dump Rfic6 write fegister *//* Attach device *//* Detach device *//* Change device state/flags *//* Attach Log *//* Share temperature struct *//* Attach svcerr *//* RTNL event *//* NDP frame *//* Recv File I/O req *//* TKIP MIC failure detected *//* MuC boot complete *//* drop BA *//* disassociate station with a given aid *//* detected RFIC abnormal reset, reboot the system *//* start Tx ADDBA REQ sequence *//* Peer RTS enable or disable *//* Dynamic WMM enable or disable *//* TDLS Events from MuCfw *//* Per-node rate training hash *//* Fixed bw command offset *//* aim to change channels at this tsf *//* tsf just after channel change completed *//* pre-switch notification to lhost in TU *//* post channel change notification *//* freqency band info *//* channel to switch to *//* status written by MuC *//* flags written by lhost *//* time slice *//* prime time count based on meas_slice *//* secondary time count based on meas_slice *//* working channel to return to *//* measurement type *//* measurement reason *//* time slice for measurement long duration *//* results structure for CCA measurement *//* The channel on which sample will be taken *//* Duration in milliseconds to stay on off channel *//* tsf at which to start sampling *//* qosnull frame for channel sampling *//* qosnull frame in phyaddr *//* the frame length of qosnull *//* the node index that qosnull frame to *//* the tsf_lo read from MAC on that qosnull frame was sent successfully *//* the large NAV in qosnull frame *//* timestamps used for precise time control and profiling *//* Smart channel selection data shared between Lhost and MuC *//* 0 or 1 *//* Data channel to return to *//* The required remain channel *//* Duration in microseconds to stay on remain channel *//* tsf at which to switch to remain channel *//* channel switch status *//* peer node mac address *//* The channel on which sample will be taken *//* microseconds, time overhead for others before start frame is sent*//* microseconds, time overhead for others after start frame is sent*//* microseconds, the time offset for sending probe_req frame
						 * after switching to off channel*//* microseconds, the time offset for sending start frame
						 * after set NETDEV_F_PAUSE_TX flag *//* microseconds, the time duration for transmitting all beacons *//* microseconds, the minimal time for waiting for the probe
						 * response frame on scanning channel *//* Duration in milliseconds to stay on scanning channel *//* written only by MuC *//* The frame sent before go scan channel,
						 * e.g. pwrsav frame in STA mode *//* Start frame in phyaddr *//* the node index that frame to *//* frame length *//* probe request frame for active scanning *//* probe request frame in phyaddr *//* the node index that frame to *//* frame length *//* The frame sent after back data channel,
						 * e.g. the frame to announce waking up in STA mode *//* Complete frame in phyaddr *//* the node index that frame to *//* frame length *//* frequency band, written by lhost *//* The off channel, "0" means to stop ocac in MuC, written by lhost*//* qosnull frame in virtual address, written by lhost *//* qosnull frame in physical address, written by lhost *//* the frame length of qosnull *//* the node index that qosnull frame to *//* the required time on off channel in one beacon interval, written by lhost *//* milliseconds, the time on off channel within on off-channel action, using
							qosnull frame with large NAV to protect the traffic *//* the fat threshold to run off-channel CAC, written by lhost *//* the traffic threshold to run off-channel CAC, written by lhost *//* the threshold for consecutive fat decrease, written by lhost *//* whether to send qosnull or not, written by lhost *//* milliseconds, the offset after beacon to halt tx, written by lhost *//* milliseconds, the offset after halt tx to switch off channel, written by lhost *//* current on which channel, written by MuC *//* the actual time on off channel, written by MuC *//* event tsf log, written by MuC *//* STA exits BMPS mode *//* in BMPS mode, and is fully powered on *//* with PM set to 0 *//* in BMPS mode, and is fully powered off *//* with PM set to 1 *//* in BMPS mode, and is transitting from *//* power-on to power-off by sending Null frame *//* with PM=1 to AP *//* in BMPS mode, and Null frame with PM=1 *//* has been sent, TX path is paused, *//* but RX patgh is still running to *//* receive packets from leaky AP *//* in BMPS mode, and is transitting from *//* power-off to power-on by sending *//* Null frame with PM=0 to AP *//* in BMPS mode, and RX chain is powered up *//* to receive beacon *//* null frame in virtual address *//* null frame in physical address *//* the frame length of null *//* the node index that null frame to *//* shared BMPS status *//* MuC fops requst *//* The following file indexes and file lists must all be kept in sync *//* header *//* assoc response *//* special-purpose state *//* The RX side of the implicit BA. Zero for no implicit RX BA *//* The TX side of the implicit BA. Zero for no implicit TX BA *//* raw beacon interval *//* Size of the implicit BAs *//* flag to disallow BBF *//* flag to disallow standard BF *//* U-APSD per-node flags matching WMM STA Qos Info field *//* Processed HT capabilities *//* Processed HT info *//* Processed VHT capabilities *//* Processed VHT operational info *//* optional rsn capabilities *//* selected unicast cipher *//* tdls peer AID allocated by AP, unique in BSS *//* key length in bytes *//* key used for xmit *//* key used for recv *//* key used for WPA group operation *//* host-based encrypt/decrypt *//* host-based enmic/demic *//* key index *//* XXX can't () right *//* XXX can't () right *//* key receive sequence counter *//* key transmit sequence counter *//* cipher *//* node cache index *//* common flags passed in by apps *//* shared between muc and lhost *//* MU group ID. 0 means the group is not used and grp_ni is empty*//* mu QMat installation status *//* QMat is not installed and not used *//* QMat is installed and used *//* QMat is installed, used but not updated *//* QMat is installed, not used and not updated *//* the index of the grp_ni[], is also the user position *//* matrix addr offsets in sram *//* stats */// _LHOST_MUC_COMM_H/*
 * (C) Copyright 2011 Quantenna Communications Inc.
 *
 * See file CREDITS for list of people who contributed to this
 * project.
 *
 * This program is free software; you can redistribute it and/or
 * modify it under the terms of the GNU General Public License as
 * published by the Free Software Foundation; either version 2 of
 * the License, or (at your option) any later version.
