EH1*//* When set to 1 LHOST formats AuC print output. It is not possible to use %s and %pM
conversion specifiers. Also the number of arguments printed are limited to 8 and therefore
stack size is limited to 32.
When set to 0 AuC formats the output, pass the formatted line to the LHOST that
prints it. *//* QTN_DEBUG_H_ *//*
 * Length of received frame that requires dcache invalidate on receive.
 * The amount that must be read is:
 * - VLAN encap case: MAX_VLANS * (LLC + 2b) + LLC
 * - 802.11 MPDU, no amsdu: LLC + max l3 depth
 * - 802.11 AMSDU: msdu header + LLC + max l3 depth
 *
 * The max of these three is the VLAN case. There is also an assumption
 * here that if VLANs are processed, there is no need to process L3 header
 *//* the eth header to be written to the packet *//* space for vlan headers (must be after eh) *//* pointer to layer 3 header in the payload *//* l3 header type (may not match eh.ether_type for 802.3 *//* to which VLAN te msdu belongs *//* first msdu in an amsdu *//* last msdu in an amsdu *//* start is decapped eh, not wireless header *//* requires 3 address bridge dest mac set *//* Frame has HT control field in the header *//*
 * Remove the LLC/SNAP header (if present) and replace with an Ethernet header
 *
 * See IEEE 802.1H for LLC/SNAP encapsulation/decapsulation.
 *   Ethernet-II SNAP header (RFC1042 for most Ethertypes)
 *   Bridge-Tunnel header (for Ethertypes ETH_P_AARP and ETH_P_IPX
 *   No encapsulation header if Ethertype < 0x600 (=length)
 *//*
	 * For EAPOL and VLAN frames we do not want to add 802.1Q header.
	 * Otherwise, the frame won't go through a driver.
	 *//*
	* Common part of the header - RFC1042 (final byte is 0x0) or
	* bridge tunnel encapsulation (final byte is 0xF8)
	*//* Pass back pointer to start of training data *//* only attempt to decap data frames *//* find qos ctrl field *//* amsdu *//* decapped length includes subframe padding */// __QTN_DECAP_H__/*
 * Copyright (c) 2011-2012 Quantenna Communications, Inc.
 * All rights reserved.
 *//*
 * The MuC TX Queuing algorithm is selected by setting
 * g_tx_queuing_alg. Values are:
 * 0 = Round robin
 * 1 = Equal airtime
 * 2 = Greedy best
 * 3 = Round robin (filling to make a power of 4)
 * x >= 4: algorithm chosen by (val % 4), with airtime
 * debugs enabled, printed every (val) seconds.
 *//* must be greater than the above to prevent stalling *//* high value for zero PER *//* add tx restrict check if this is increased *//* sw retry when the sending frames are suspended *//* allow MSDUs to time out? *//* allow aggregation? *//* dbm *//* + top byte is the FD to dump *//* msecs *//* counter for delay in RFIC6 500Mhz *//* Enable SW workaround for short range association *//* Hardware supports automatic RX gain *//* Cumulative gain for all rx pkts *//* Number of pkts for which cumulative gain was considered *//* off channel params *//* If higher than this value, increase the CCA threshold *//* If higher than this value, increase the CCA threshold *//* The max cca threshold we can set *//* Max packets per second in Tx restrict mode *//* RTS threshold *//* enable/disable 1bit *//* Get/Set carrier ID *//* promote AC_BE traffic to vo/vi *//* turn on/off TxBF IOT with non QTN node *//* promote AC_BE traffic to vo/vi *//* enable-disable 1ss AMSDU support - Non-qtn clients *//* manual update VHT NDPA duration, if it is 0, then HW auto update *//* Tx operation count threshold to a SU TxBF station *//* Tx operation count threshold to a MU TxBF station *//* Configure HT-VHT / Legacy frame format for NDP announcements *//* enable default 1ss matrix feature *//* the threshold to install defalut 1ss matrix *//* enable/disable MU Tx *//* L2 external filter *//* L2 external filter port *//* enable/disable auto cs threshold *//* sync rx reorder window on receiving BAR *//* Add all new fields before this one *//* Please keep this structure in sync with qtn_global_param *//* defined(MUC_BUILD) *//*
 * SKBs on the power save queue are tagged with an age and timed out.  We reuse the
 * hardware checksum field in the mbuf packet header to store this data.
 *//* RFIC chip ID *//* MU-MIMO WMAC index *//* _QTN_GLOBAL_MUC_H *//*SH0
*******************************************************************************
