EH1*//*
 * Enable installation of a fixed Q matrix in place of the derived ones.
 * The matrix should be put in the file drivers/qdrv/fixedqmat.h
 * The format of the data should be word values comma delimited.
 *//* Until we get 2 tx antennas working on a 2x4 station *//*
 * Comment this line to disable locking.
 * Or set to 1 to enable manual locking.
 * Or set to 0 to enable hw-centric automatic locking.
 *//* VHTTXBFTBD - 11ac BF enabled by default *//* Use sw generated VHT BF path *//* #define TXBF_VHT_SW_FEEDBACK *//* #define TXBF_VHT_SW_UNCOMPRESSED *//* for debugging *//* Expansion Matrix Modes *//* Enable (1) both hw and sw generated VHT BF feedback, used for debugging *//* Tx BF buffer for the frame is free *//* The frame is stored in Tx BF buffer for processing and can not be released*//* Not used *//* NDP only. The frame is being processed by DSP *//* DSP completes frame processing *//* For action frame only. Action frame is stored in action frame cache *//* Envy *//* 2 stream Ruby *//* 4 stream non-tone grouping Ruby *//* 4 stream tone grouping Ruby and later *//*
 * Version 4 means the action frames generated are now standards compliant
 * and the BF parameters are derived from the various fields and association
 * exchange, rather than from using a new version for each combination
 *//*
 * These structures are shared between Linux, MuC and DSP.
 *//* Beamforming message types *//* Number of 10ms timeslots used on the DSP to process feedback *//* We leave backward compatibility here. As SU token value was randomly chosen as 0x33
we now say when bit 5 is set it indicates SU sounding. *//* TODO: Needs reworking. Some fields (at least mu_grp_id) are used only by
distinct message type *//* Chaining for retry on mbox busy *//* Cache aligned *//* Compq format BB0 20 bits *//* Interleaved BB1 12 bits *//* Compq format BB0 12 bits *//* Interleaved BB1 20 bits *//*
 * Maximum streams supported for different matrix types
 *//*
 * Default decimation used for matrices in Q memory. Some matrices
 * may use more decimation if space is a problem
 *//* in seconds  *//* Assumes NG 1 matrices *//*
 * Matrix sizes for NG 1 matrices
 *//*
 * Q matrix defines for 80 MHz nodes using NG 1
 *//*
 * Q matrix defines for 80 MHz nodes using NG 2
 *//*
 * Q matrix defines for 40 MHz nodes using NG 1
 *//*
 * Defines for dividing Q memory into slots for nodes using standard BF
 *//*
 * Defines for fixed matrix (BBF and default) sizes
 *//*
 * Fixed 2x4 node matrix definitions
 *//*
 * 80MHz 2x4 matrices need to start in normal BF area to fit,
 * this is OK, as they are used on the station only at present
 *//*
 * Fixed default matrix offset definitions
 *//* number of tones for fixed matrices *//*
 * BBF slot and matrix offset definitions
 *
 * For each slot there is space for the probed matrix, plus the 1, 2 and 3 streams
 * matrices for the index being used by that node
 *//* 80MHz Mode *//* Locking is disabled or manual locking *//* Automatic, hw-centric locking. *//* should be 64 bytes aligned (expmat ptr in TxVector drops lower 5 bits)*/// TODO: describe bodies as 2 dimensional arrays/* structure to hold MU group qmatrix info *//* set to 1 when it is occupied, 0 indicates it is free *//* MU group id *//* Token *//* user position 0 AID *//* user position 1 AID *//* Number of following Q matrix elements *//* matrix starting addresses in sram *//* Multiple of 20 MHz channels *//*TXBF_COMMON_H_*//*
 * (C) Copyright 2011 Quantenna Communications Inc.
 *
 * See file CREDITS for list of people who contributed to this
 * project.
 *
 * This program is free software; you can redistribute it and/or
 * modify it under the terms of the GNU General Public License as
 * published by the Free Software Foundation; either version 2 of
 * the License, or (at your option) any later version.
 *
 * This program is distributed in the hope that it will be useful,
 * but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied warranty of
 * MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE. See the
 * GNU General Public License for more details.
 *
 * You should have received a copy of the GNU General Public License
 * along with this program; if not, write to the Free Software
 * Foundation, Inc., 59 Temple Place, Suite 330, Boston,
 * MA 02111-1307 USA
 *//*
 * QTN_MAX_MU_SND_NODES nodes (6) + QTN_MAX_SND_NODES (10) + 3 for IPC cmd 19.
 * This value still causes buffer allocation failure, which is probably due to bad DSP performance.
 * With 3 more there is no allocation failure for 4 STAs case.
 *//* MU group install/delete IPC from DSP to LHost *//* Per-node DSP stats *//* Total number of feedbacks received *//* Number of SU feedbacks *//* Number of MU group selection feedbacks *//* Number of MU precoding feedbacks *//* Number of bad feedbacks, i.e. those that are not met SU nor MU criteria *//*
	 * Number of feedbacks that were not places into the cache due to any reason. Counters for two reasons
	 * are just below
	 *//* The number of MU feedback not placed into the cache as the previous one has not been exprired *//* The number of MU feedback not placed into the cache due to cache is locked *//*
	 * The number of precoding feedback was released unused, i.e. not participated in QMat calculation.
	 * It means the buddy feedback either have not been received or received after cache expiration time
	 *//* The number of MU feedback for which dsp_qmat_check_act_len is failed *//* Number or QMat currently installed *//*
 * Number of times dsp_sram_qmat_num becomes negative. Non zero value signals that the number
 * of QMat de-installation is more than the number of installations. This is an error condition but not a critical one
 *//* Interrupts *//* registers *//* The number of failed group installations *//* Per-MU group DSP stats *//* The number of successful group installations *//* The number of successful QMat installations *//* The number of failed QMat installations *//* Group's AID 0 *//* Group's AID 1 *//* Group's rank *//*
	 * Distribution (histogram) of MU QMat copying time
	 0:  0- 3us
	 1:  4- 7us
	 ...............
	 3: 12+ us
	 *//*
	 * Distribution (histogram) of MU QMat calculation and installation time
	 0:  0- 3ms
	 1:  4- 7ms
	 ...............
	 3: 12+ ms
	 *//* Structure be used for txbf message box *//* Write index in txbf_msg_bufs array. Updated only by a sender *//* Debug verbosity level *//* Used for testing to set rank for STA pairs manually *//* in case of adding algorithms above please update below equation accordingly *//* Initialize SPI controller, keep IRQ disabled *//* Ack, and keep IRQ disabled *//*
	 * Only single interrupt is supported now.
	 * If need to support more interrupts then something like
	 * 'status' in RAM, guarded by semaphores has to be implemented.
	 * This should be avoided, as it is performance penalty.
	 */// #if !defined(MUC_BUILD) && !defined(DSP_BUILD) && !defined(AUC_BUILD)/* Linux target *//* Linux target *//*value is not important*//* Locking is disabled *//* Manual, sw-centric locking. *//* Automatic, hw-centric locking.
	 * Hw locks FFT memory automatically after the NDP packet is received.
	 * No need to explicitely lock FFT.
	 *//* Locking is disabled *//* Manual, sw-centric locking. *//* Automatic, hw-centric locking. *//*
* qtn_txbf_mbox can be used to set parameters for DSP core from other cores.
* Ideally this way should be reworked but until it happens lets use dedicated macros to access such parameters
* to distibuish this qtn_txbf_mbox usage purpose from others (IPC, BF feedbacks exchange)
*/// #ifndef __ASSEMBLY__// #ifndef __QTN_TXBF_MBOX_H/**
