 *//* direct sequence spread spectrum *//* frequency hopping *//* frequency division multiplexing *//* high rate OFDM, aka turbo mode *//* HT - full GI *//* more common nomenclature *//*
 * XXX not really a mode; there are really multiple PHY's
 * Please update ieee80211_chanflags when the definition of
 * ieee80211_phymode changed
 *//* autoselect *//* 5GHz, OFDM *//* 2GHz, CCK *//* 2GHz, OFDM *//* 2GHz, GFSK *//* 5GHz, OFDM, 2x clock dynamic turbo *//* 2GHz, OFDM, 2x clock  dynamic turbo*//* 5GHz, HT20 *//* 2GHz, HT20 *//* 2GHz HT40 *//* 5GHz HT40 *//* 5GHz VHT20 *//* 5GHz VHT40 *//* 5GHz VHT80 *//* 5GHz VHT160 *//* Always keep this last *//*
#define IEEE80211_BM_11A	(1 << IEEE80211_MODE_11A)
#define IEEE80211_BM_11B	(1 << IEEE80211_MODE_11B)
#define IEEE80211_BM_11G	(1 << IEEE80211_MODE_11B)
#define IEEE80211_BM_11NA	(1 << IEEE80211_MODE_11B)
#define IEEE80211_BM_11NG	(1 << IEEE80211_MODE_11B)
#define IEEE80211_BM_11NG_PLUS	(1 << IEEE80211_MODE_11B)
#define IEEE80211_BM_11NG_MINUS	(1 << IEEE80211_MODE_11B)
#define IEEE80211_BM_11NA_PLUS	(1 << IEEE80211_MODE_11B)
#define IEEE80211_BM_11NA_MINUS	(1 << IEEE80211_MODE_11B)
*//* infrastructure station *//* IBSS (adhoc) station *//* Old lucent compatible adhoc demo *//* Software Access Point *//* Monitor mode *//* WDS link *//*
 * 802.11n
 *//* or 80+80 Mhz *//* no protection *//* CTS to self *//* RTS-CTS *//* CWM (Channel Width Management) Information *//* Configuration *//* CWM mode *//* CWM Extension Channel Offset *//* CWM Extension Channel Protection Mode *//* CWM Extension Channel Protection Spacing *//* State *//* CWM channel width *//* ieee rate *//* Holds the fixed rate information for each VAP *//*
 * 802.11g protection mode.
 *//* no protection *//* CTS to self *//* RTS-CTS *//*
 * Authentication mode.
 *//* open *//* shared-key *//* 802.1x *//* auto-select/accept *//* NB: these are used only for ioctls *//* WPA/RSN w/ 802.1x/PSK *//*
 * Roaming mode is effectively who controls the operation
 * of the 802.11 state machine when operating as a station.
 * State transitions are controlled either by the driver
 * (typically when management frames are processed by the
 * hardware/firmware), the host (auto/normal operation of
 * the 802.11 layer), or explicitly through ioctl requests
 * when applications like wpa_supplicant want control.
 *//* driver/hardware control *//* 802.11 layer control *//* application control *//*
 * Scanning mode controls station scanning work; this is
 * used only when roaming mode permits the host to select
 * the bss to join/channel to use.
 *//* driver/hardware control *//* 802.11 layer selects best *//* take first suitable candidate *//* ba state describes the block ack state. block ack should only be sent if
 * ba state is set to established
 *//* ba type describes the block acknowledgement type *//* power index definition *//* MFP capabilities (ieee80211w) *//*
 * Channels are specified by frequency and attributes.
 *//* setting in Mhz *//* see below *//* IEEE channel number *//* maximum regulatory tx power in dBm *//* maximum tx power in dBm for the current bandwidth with beam-forming off *//* minimum tx power in dBm *//* backup max tx power for short-range workaround *//* backup min tx power for short-range workaround *//* the maximum powers for different cases *//* number that radar signal has been detected on this channel *//* howmany(IEEE80211_CHAN_MAX, NBBY) *//* token for ``any channel'' *//* Move to channel 36 for mute test *//* bits 0-3 are for private use by drivers *//* channel attributes *//* Turbo channel *//* CCK channel *//* OFDM channel *//* 2 GHz spectrum channel. *//* 5 GHz spectrum channel *//* Only passive scan allowed *//* Dynamic CCK-OFDM channel *//* GFSK channel (FHSS PHY) *//* Status: Radar found on channel *//* 11a static turbo channel only *//* Half rate channel *//* Quarter rate channel *//* HT 20 channel *//* HT 40 with ext channel above *//* HT 40 with ext channel below *//* HT 40 with ext channel above/below *//* Configuration: DFS-required channel *//* Status: CAC completed *//* VHT 80 *//* Status: Off-channel CAC completed *//* Status: Valid CAC is in progress *//* Configuration: weather channel for 20MHz *//* Configuration: weather channel for 40MHz *//* Configuration: weather channel for 80MHz *//*11AC - 40MHZ flags *//* VHT 40 with ext channel above *//* VHT 40 with ext channel below *//* VHT 40 with ext channel above/below *//*11AC - 20MHZ flags *//* VHT 20 channel *//* below are channel ext attributes(ic_ext_flags) *//* 11AC - 80MHZ flags *//*
 * Useful combinations of channel characteristics.
 *///(((_c)->ic_flags & IEEE80211_CHAN_ANYN))/* mode specific macros *//* ni_chan encoding for FH phy *//* Peer RTS config *//* Dynamic WMM *//*
 * 802.11 rate set.
 *//* 802.11 standard *//* Non 11n Rates *//* max rates we'll handle *//* Total number of 802.11n rates *//* For legacy hardware - leaving it as is for now *///#define IEEE80211_RATE_IDX_ENTRY(val, idx) (val&(0xff<<(8*idx))>>(idx*8))/*
 * 11n A-MPDU & A-MSDU limits . XXX
 *//*
 * 11ac MPDU size limit
 *//* enough for mpdu header 36 + crypto 20 + fcs 4 *//*
 * 11n and 11ac AMSDU sizes
 *//*
 * 11n MCS set limits
 *//*
 * B0-B2: MCS index, B3-B6: MCS set index, B8: BASIC RATE
 *//* index number in the set will be (_i - 1) if (_i != 0) *//* rate table index = (MCS set index << 3) + MCS index *//* Supported rate label *//* integer portion of HT rates *//* Number of legacy rates *//* Total rates = Legacy + 11n *//* Number of legacy rates *//* Total rates = Legacy + 11n *//* rssi thresh for 11a bss *//* for 11g sta in 11b bss *//* for 11b sta *//* rate thresh for 11a bss *//* for 11g sta in 11b bss *//* for 11b sta *//* HT capabilities *//* Number of Tx spatial streams *//* Number of Rx stbc streams *//* HT power save mode *//* MPDU density *//* Max MSDU size *//* maximum rx A-MPDU factor *//* HT MCS set *//* HT max data rate *//* HT extended capability *//* HT MCS params *//* HT transmit beamforming capabilities *//* control channel *//* ht ie byte 1 *//* ht ie byte 2 *//* ht ie byte 3 *//* ht ie byte 4 *//* ht ie byte 5 *//* signal granularity *//* external channel offset *//* operational mode *//* basic MCS set *//* VHT capabilities MIB *//* Maximum MPDU Length B0-1 *//* Supported Channel Width Set B2-3 *//* RX STBC B8-10 *//* RX STS B13-15 *//* SOUNDING DIM B16-18 *//* Maximum A-MPDU Length exponent B23-25 *//* 2^(13 + Max A-MPDU) -1 *//* (2^13) -1 *//* (2^14) -1 *//* (2^15) -1 *//* (2^16) -1 *//* (2^17) -1 *//* (2^18) -1 *//* (2^19) -1 *//* (2^20) -1 *//* VHT link Adaptation capable B26-27 *//* VHT MCS supported */// Spatial stream not supported/* VHT NSS *//* VHT capability macros *//* VHT Operation element *//* VHT Operation Information subfields *//* VHT Operating Mode Notification element *//* Max number of MU groups *//* Max number of nodes in a MU group *//* GROUP IDs which are used for SU PPDU as per IEEE P802.11ac/D5.0,
 * chapter 9.17a Group ID and partial AID in VHT PPDUs  *//* VHT MU membership & user position arrays *//* Max number of nodes currently supported *//* category identifier *//* action identifier *//* TID *//* sequence number of first frame to be block acked *//* fragment number of first frame to be block acked *//* block ack type *//* suggested re-order buffer size *//* block ack timeout if no transfer *//* TID *//* sequence number of first frame to be block acked *//* fragment number of first frame to be block acked *//* block ack type *//* actual re-order buffer size *//* block ack negotiation status *//* negotiated block ack timeout if no transfer *//* TID *//* block ack termination reason *//* initiator/ recipient of block ack negotiation *//* number of space time streams, Nc *//* number of transmit chains, Nr *//* SNR for received space time streams *//* size of beamforming matrices in bytes *//* pointer to beamforming matrices *//* bwmode = 0 for 20Mhz and 1 for 40 M *//* switched channel width *//* new power mode *//* power save enabled *//* antenna selection: bit number corresponds
									to antenna number *//* Nc in received beamforming matrices *//* Nr in received beamforming matrices *//* Channel Width 0=20, 1 =40 *//* Ng in received beamforming matrices *//* Nb in received beamforming matrices *//* SNR as seen by sender of action frame *//* pointer to beamforming matrices,
										contents must be copied *//**
 * The following structure definitions are for passing in data to the
 * management send function to generate action frames for VSP.
 *//* dialog token *//* measurement token *//* 1: autonomous report *//* TPC actions *//* .5 dBm units *//* kill radio *//* max DTIM period *//* min DTIM period *//* default DTIM period *//* max beacon interval (TU's) *//* min beacon interval (TU's) *//* default beacon interval (TU's) *//* _NET80211__IEEE80211_H_ *//*-
