 *//* element ID *//* length in byte *//* Op Mode *//*
 * 802.11w timeout information IE
 *//* IEEE80211_ELEMID_TIMEOUT_INT *//* Timeout Interval Type *//* in tus *//*
 * Add the Quantenna OUI to a frame
 *//*
 * AUTH management packets
 *
 *	octet algo[2]
 *	octet seq[2]
 *	octet status[2]
 *	octet chal.id
 *	octet chal.length
 *	octet chal.text[253]
 *//*
 * Reason codes
 *
 * Unlisted codes are reserved
 *//* TDLS teardown due to peer unreachable *//* TDLS teardown for unspecified reason *//* Wakeup sched rejected/alternative *//* Wakeup sched rejected *//* Security disabled *//* Unacceptable lifetime *//* Not in same BSS *//* Invalid contents of RSNIE *//* Quantenna *//* 40bit *//* 24bit *//* 1 octet *//* CRC-32 *//* number of key ids *//*
 * 802.11i defines an extended IV for use with non-WEP ciphers.
 * When the EXTIV bit is set in the key id byte an additional
 * 4 bytes immediately follow the IV for TKIP.  For CCMP the
 * EXTIV bit is likewise set but the 8 bytes represent the
 * CCMP header rather than IV+extended-IV.
 *//* extended IV length *//* CCMP header *//* trailing MIC *//* ICV *//*
 * Maximum acceptable MTU is:
 *	IEEE80211_MAX_LEN - WEP overhead - CRC -
 *		QoS overhead - RSN/WPA overhead
 * Min is arbitrarily chosen > IEEE80211_MIN_LEN.  The default
 * mtu is Ethernet-compatible; it's set by ether_ifattach.
 *//*
 * RTS frame length parameters.  The default is specified in
 * the 802.11 spec.  The max may be wrong for jumbo frames.
 *//*
 * Regulatory extension identifier for country IE.
 *//*
 * IEEE 802.11 timer synchronization function (TSF) timestamp length
 *//*
 * 802.11n defines
 *//* ACM parameter *//* AIFSN parameters *//* cwmin in exponential form *//* cwmax in exponential form *//* txopLimit *//* No-Ack Policy: 0=ack, 1=no-ack *//* use for explicit BA establishing, size and throughput is moderate *//* use for implicit BA, large size to support large aggregates and high throughput *//*value assignment for the little-endian*//* 32 bits to 32 bits *//* value assignment *//* 16 bits to 16 bits *//* 32 bits to 32 bits *//* 8 bits to 32 bits *//* 16 bits to 32 bits *//* 32 bits to 64 bits *//*
 * IEEE802.11w spec - Table 8-38 and section 11.1.7
 *//* QTN Extender *//* 0 = Plain WDS; No WDS Extender *//* 1 = MBS-Master Base Station *//* 2 = RBS-Repeater/Remote Base Station *//* MU MIMO *//* 0 - Default internal group. 1 - 31 User configurable group id *//* _NET80211_IEEE80211_H_ *//*-
