to sync up with SIOCRDEVSTATS in /linux/sockios.h *//* This command is used to support sub-ioctls *//*
 * ioctl command IEEE80211_IOCTL_EXT is used to support sub-ioctls.
 * The following lists the sub-ioctl numbers
 *
 *//* Command to set the SOC addr of the STB to VAP for recording *//* Set TDLS Operation *//* Deactive DFS channels *//* device name *//* operating mode *//* see below *//* allocate unique mac/bssid *//* Do not setup the station beacon timers *//* Search for power table in bootcfg only *//* Search for power table in bootcfg at first, if not find, then search /etc/ *//* Search for power table in /etc/ at first, if not find, then search bootcfg *//* Search for power table in /etc/ only *//* APPIEBUF related definitions *//* Management frame type to which application IE is added *//* the beaconing schemes - the mapping between 8 VAPs and 4 HW TX queues for beacon *//*
	 * Scheme 0 - default
	 * VAP0/VAP4 - HW queue0
	 * VAP1/VAP5 - HW queue1
	 * VAP2/VAP6 - HW queue2
	 * VAP3/VAP7 - HW queue3
	 *//*
	 * Scheme 1:
	 * VAP0/VAP1 - HW queue0
	 * VAP2/VAP3 - HW queue1
	 * VAP4/VAP5 - HW queue2
	 * VAP6/VAP7 - HW queue3
	 *//*
 * This enum must be kept in sync with tdls_operation_string.
 * enum ieee80211_tdls_operation - values for tdls_oper callbacks
 * @IEEE80211_TDLS_DISCOVERY_REQ: Send a TDLS discovery request
 * @IEEE80211_TDLS_SETUP: Setup TDLS link
 * @IEEE80211_TDLS_TEARDOWN: Teardown a TDLS link which is already established
 * @IEEE80211_TDLS_ENABLE_LINK: Enable TDLS link
 * @IEEE80211_TDLS_DISABLE_LINK: Disable TDLS link
 * @IEEE80211_TDLS_ENABLE: Enable TDLS function
 * @IEEE80211_TDLS_DISABLE: Disable TDLS function
 * @IEEE80211_TDLS_PTI_REQ: Send a TDLS Peer Traffic Indication Frame
 *//* Destination address of tdls action *//* TDLS action frame type *//* Statu code *//* Dialog token *//* Subsequent IEs length*//* Subsequent IEs *//* management frame type for which buffer is added *//* application-supplied buffer length *//* flags here is used to check whether QTN pairing IE exists *//* application-supplied IE(s) *//* Action frame payload *//* action frame payload length *//* action frame payload data *//* Structure used to send action frame from hostapd *//* action frame category *//* action frame action *//* Flags ORed by application to set filter for receiving management frames *//* used to check the valid filter bits *//* management frame filter type *//* Tx Restrict *//* Compatibility fix bitmap for various vendor peer *//**
 * Structure contains data of wds extender event.
 * @name will always be "QTN-WDS-EXT"
 * @cmd message type.
 * @mac specify wds peer mac address
 * @link_status specify the wds link state.
 * @ie_len when the message contains an wds extender IE, ie_len is larger than 0.
 *//**
	 * Number of dropped data packets failed to transmit through
	 * wireless media for each traffic category(TC).
	 *//**
	 * Number of sent data packets that transmit through
	 * wireless media for each traffic category(TC).
