EH1*//* microseconds *//* SCS (ACI/CCI Detection and Mitigation) APIs *//* param change *//* seconds *//* metric *//* metric *//* milliseconds, limited by max NAV reservation *//* milliseconds *//* milliseconds *//* seconds *//* seconds *//* seconds *//* packet number *//* packet number *//* packet number *//* ms *//* ms *//* ms *//* count *//* count *//*
 * Packet rate threshold is determined by how many packets we can hold in buffer without drop
 * during off-channel period. It is limited by:
 * - sw queue length of each node/tid
 * - global resource shared by all node/tid, such as tqew descriptors and msdu headers.
 * Current value doesn't apply to the scenario when tqew descriptors are already used up by large
 * number of stations.
 *//* margin = 128 + hw ring size *//* assume qtn peer *//* db *//* db *//* db *//* seconds *//* seconds *//* seconds *//* kbps *//* unit: 100kbps *//* unit: 100kbps *//* unit: 100kbps *//* seconds *//* seconds *//* milliseconds *//* microseconds *//* microseconds *//* microseconds *//* microseconds, the time duration for transmitting all beacons *//* seconds *//* seconds *//* off-channel, use smoothing and omit current channel *//* co-channel mode *//* like off-channel but include current channel *//* OCAC (Off-channel CAC) APIs *//* milliseconds *//* milliseconds *//* milliseconds *//* milliseconds *//* milliseconds *//* milliseconds *//* milliseconds *//* seconds *//* seconds *//* seconds *//* seconds *//* seconds *//* seconds *//* seconds *//* seconds *//* seconds *//* seconds *//* seconds *//* seconds *//* percent *//* percent *//* percent *//* percent *//* percent *//* percent *//* milliseconds *//* milliseconds *//* milliseconds *//* milliseconds *//* milliseconds *//* milliseconds *//* on *//* percent *//* percent *//* percent *//* percent *//* percent *//* percent *//* seconds *//* seconds *//* seconds *//* TUs *//* TUs *//* TUs *//* seconds *//* seconds *//* seconds *//* microseconds *//* enable power management *//* disable power management *//* ps poll *//* U-APSD SP *//* Set per-TID flag(muc) *//* per VAP TX BA est control *//* Common definitions for flags used to indicate ieee80211_node's states *//* authorized for data *//* QoS enabled *//* ERP enabled *//* HT enabled *//* NB: this must have the same value as IEEE80211_FC1_PWR_MGT *//* power save mode enabled *//* STA out of PS, getting delivery *//* power save ps poll mode *//* authentication ref held *//* this node needs to use 2 TX chain only, for IOT purpose *//* this node is the wds peer in a wds vap *//* VHT enabled *//* indicate tpc capability *//* Common definitions for ext_flags *//* Should sending PTI request to peer *//* PTI request xmit to peer but not responsed *//* U-APSD SP in progress *//* PTI response frame received *//* authorized for TDLS link data *//* Mask for TDLS PTI bits *//* reserve the low values for internal use *//* hw limitation for 128 node mode *//* for maximum 8 TIDs *//* values below this are used for "bad apple" nodes *//* Quantenna specific flags (ni_qtn_flags), do not modify in Auc *//* restricted tx enabled *//* use RTS to confirm node is lost *//* node support TX amsdu *//*
 * Bits that can be updated again by Lhost after association creation. Explicit definition helps
 * avoid overwriting bits maintained by MuC itself.
 *//* QTN bandwidth definition - make sure this is up-to-date with regards
 * to txbf_common.h
 *//* Invalid value to indicate mailbox is disabled *//* WoWLAN APIs *//*
 * Definitions relating to individual fields from phy_stats,
 * shared between the Q driver and the APIs.
 *//*
 * Error Sum needs to be reported together with the corresponding Number of
 * Symbols; getting them in separate operations would introduce a race condition
 * where the Error Sum and the Number of Symbols came from different
 * PHY stat blocks.
 *//* only for little endian *//* for MuC and Auc which don't support "X" *//*
 * VSP/QTM
 * Macro TOPAZ_QTM is used to help identify changes between original VSP and QTM.
 * In Lhost kernel driver, it must be used within CONFIG_QVSP(in kernel .config).
 * CONFIG_QVSP	TOPAZ_QTM	ruby		topaz
 * Y		1		invalid		*QTM works
 * Y		0		*VSP works	VSP alive but doesn't work for HDP
 * N		1		invalid		*no VSP/QTM
 * N		0		*no VSP		no VSP/QTM, and no QTM changes in MuC and AuC
 * So generally, sololy changing CONFIG_QVSP works for both ruby and topaz as indicated by *.
 * But to throughly clean QTM code in AuC and MuC, disable TOPAZ_QTM in topaz below.
 *//**@addtogroup DFSAPIs
 *@{*//**
 * Reason for channel change
 *//**
	 * Reason is unknown
	 *//**
	 * Smart channel selection
	 *//**
	 * Radar detection
	 *//**
	 * Channel set by user
	 *//**
	 * Configuration change
	 *//**
	 * Scan initiated by user
	 *//**
	 * Off-channel CAC
	 *//**
	 * Channel switch announcement
	 *//**
